  "notes": "⚠ **The 1991 record only** — the research is explicit that his post-1993 Hieroglyphics work belongs to the boom-bap lane, so the modelled window is a single year and this entry should not be read as covering his catalogue. Oakland P-Funk-sample rap produced inside the Ice Cube camp, and the one parameter the research puts above all others is the bass: \"sampled P-Funk bass, syncopated and busy — bass carries the groove's personality here more than the drums\". That is the lowest `followRootsProb` in this batch (0.35), the widest register (28–50), a full passing-tone set and `anticipationProb` at 0.42. The harmony is inherited from the source loops — flat-7 vamps with occasional jazzier ii–V colour — so `dorian` and `mixolydian` carry the scale weight, `i–VII` sits at weight 5, and a `ii–v–i` family is present at weight 2 for the jazzier cuts. The research says 4-bar loops with *one* chord change, which is why `maxChords` is 3 and `2_bars_per_chord` leads the harmonic rhythm. \"Rolling keys, lazy horn loops, placid guitar plucks\" is `warm_keys` at 4–7 notes a bar over swung sample-derived drums (`swing` 0.62, `quantizeStrength` 0.8) with five perc lanes for the loop-plus-live-percussion method. ⚠ `confidence` is `medium` per the research's high-medium rating; **the inferred parameter is the ii–v–i family's weight** — the research says jazzier colour appears without saying how often. ⚠ The bass ceiling came down from 50 to 46 so it stays under a chord part that starts at 47 — `coherence.rs` requires the highest bass note to sit at or below the lowest chord note, and this model overlapped by 4.",
